{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 202, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At very small learning rates training is under-converged in 243 epochs, so increasing the step size yields large gains."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At already-large learning rates Adam diverges, so further increases sharply reduce accuracy."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Large batches give lower-noise gradients and fewer updates, so they benefit more from (and tolerate) larger learning rates."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Tiny batches already make many noisy updates, so raising the learning rate adds instability rather than progress."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Once the L2 penalty is large, increasing it further causes severe underfitting, unlike the negligible effect at tiny alphas."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper networks are more prone to divergence at high learning rates, making added depth harmful there."}, {"edit_param": "width", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Wider layers amplify update magnitudes at large step sizes, worsening instability."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training when the learning rate is too